> The effects of scrolls also depend on the buc (Blessed / Uncursed /
> Cursed) status of the scroll. So even if it has the same name, the
> effect will be quite different for a blessed scroll than a cursed one.
>
> But if you have two scrolls with the same buc status with the same name
> then they will have similar effects.

More specifically, if you have two (or more) scrolls that stack in
your inventory -- that is, they are listed in your inventory under a
single letter like "s - 2 scrolls labeled FOO" -- then they will have
the same effect.

However, if the scrolls do *not* stack -- that is, if they are listed
separately as "s - a scroll labeled FOO; t - a scroll labeled FOO" --
then they're different in some small but significant way (such as one
being blessed and the other not) and may have different effects.

In most cases blessed and uncursed scrolls have similar effects, only
differing in magnitude.  Cursed scrolls, however, may have different
or even completely opposite effects.  You can tell if a scroll is
cursed by dropping it and seeing if your pet will voluntarily step on
it or pick it up -- if it does, it isn't cursed.  (Note that pets will
also avoid scrolls of scare monster whether they're cursed or not.)

Dropping the scrolls on an altar will also work, and will directly
tell you whether they are blessed, uncursed or cursed.  However,
scrolls that have been tested that way will not stack with scrolls
that haven't been, even if both actually are identical.

